WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.900
Imagine, um, just for a moment, that you are standing in this big, empty field.

00:04.960 --> 00:06.040
Okay, setting the scene.

00:06.320 --> 00:16.220
Yeah, exactly. The wind is blowing, the grass is high, and you have just been given the most daunting, like, truly terrifying assignment in human history.

00:16.400 --> 00:16.960
Which is?

00:17.100 --> 00:20.880
You are tasked with rebuilding society from absolute scratch.

00:21.080 --> 00:23.440
Oh, wow. That is a lot of pressure.

00:23.440 --> 00:30.360
Right. Every institution, every law, every government building, every currency you've ever known has completely vanished.

00:31.120 --> 00:32.580
You have a totally blank slate.

00:32.720 --> 00:33.760
Just you in the grass.

00:34.060 --> 00:36.140
Yeah, and millions of people are looking at you waiting.

00:36.440 --> 00:41.200
So what is the very first thing your new government absolutely must do?

00:41.440 --> 00:47.140
I mean, most people would probably sit down by a campfire and, I don't know, try to draft a constitution.

00:47.640 --> 00:51.300
Right, or maybe you start passing laws to keep people from stealing from each other.

00:51.300 --> 00:53.600
Or you figure out a way to collect taxes.

00:53.920 --> 00:55.900
Or maybe you just crown a leader, you know?

00:56.180 --> 01:01.080
Find the smartest or the strongest person and say, uh, okay, you're in charge, tell us what to do.

01:01.600 --> 01:06.500
Exactly. Because most of us, when we think about government, we immediately jump to the language of authority.

01:06.880 --> 01:10.580
Yeah, we think about who has the power to tell other people what to do.

01:11.100 --> 01:13.000
It's completely natural that we go there.

01:13.160 --> 01:17.020
I mean, our entire historical vocabulary for politics is built around this.

01:17.020 --> 01:29.720
Oh, absolutely. If you trace it all the way from Plato in ancient Greece, through Thomas Hobbes and John Locke, right up to modern political science, it's all built around this central pillar of sovereignty.

01:30.120 --> 01:35.580
We are just obsessed with the idea of legitimacy as this form of, like, rightful domination.

01:35.940 --> 01:38.140
We constantly ask who ought to rule.

01:38.400 --> 01:43.060
And by what moral or historical right do they hold that power over the rest of us?

01:43.180 --> 01:46.440
We treat government like it's a throne that someone gets to sit on.

01:46.440 --> 01:49.500
But today's deep dive is going to completely dismantle that throne.

01:49.960 --> 01:54.320
We are looking at a genuinely mind-bending monograph from 2026.

01:54.520 --> 01:56.400
Right. The one by the researcher known as Flyxion.

01:56.600 --> 02:00.780
Yes. It's called Constitutional Cybernetics, a control theoretic theory of government.

02:01.220 --> 02:09.040
And the mission for this deep dive is to completely rewire how you think about politics, human rights, and even democracy itself.

02:09.040 --> 02:13.880
We are basically taking that traditional language of authority and legitimacy and tossing it out the window.

02:14.400 --> 02:15.180
Right out the window.

02:15.180 --> 02:20.500
In its place, we are bringing in the language of cybernetics and control theory.

02:20.740 --> 02:24.180
Which sounds super sci-fi, but it's incredibly grounded.

02:24.600 --> 02:25.760
Okay, let's unpack this.

02:26.280 --> 02:33.200
The core premise we are starting with is that a government is not a static institution that rules over you.

02:33.360 --> 02:33.600
Right.

02:33.780 --> 02:39.860
It is a dynamic, continuously operating feedback loop of estimation and control.

02:39.860 --> 02:45.340
Yeah. Flickrise is really demanding a radical fundamental shift in our perspective here.

02:45.700 --> 02:46.100
How so?

02:46.100 --> 02:55.800
Well, if we genuinely want to understand what a government is and why it fails or succeeds, we have to stop looking at static snapshots of institutions.

02:56.060 --> 02:57.840
Like organizational charts and that sort of thing.

02:57.840 --> 02:59.560
Exactly. We have to stop looking at those.

02:59.560 --> 03:06.400
We are shifting entirely away from asking who ought to rule to asking what any governing system must actually accomplish in real time.

03:06.600 --> 03:09.080
Basically, how to keep society from crashing into a wall.

03:09.320 --> 03:12.820
You got it. It frames governance purely as an engineering problem.

03:12.880 --> 03:14.860
So it's not about morality or divine right.

03:14.860 --> 03:16.880
No, it's about survival.

03:17.880 --> 03:28.960
If a society is going to survive the next century, it has to continually observe itself, figure out what state it's currently in, compare that to where it wants to be, and then take corrective action.

03:29.160 --> 03:32.980
So it's not about issuing grand moral commands from on high.

03:33.020 --> 03:40.860
Exactly. It's about maintaining a viable trajectory through an incredibly unpredictable, hostile environment.

03:40.860 --> 03:47.100
To really grasp how massive this shift is, I want to look at this amazing historical coincidence.

03:48.080 --> 03:54.120
Or honestly, maybe it's less of a coincidence and more of a hidden truth that's just been buried in the dictionary for thousands of years.

03:54.200 --> 03:56.700
Oh, the etymology thing. Yeah, this is wild.

03:56.800 --> 04:00.320
When I was reading through your notes on this, I had to stop and look it up because it blew my mind.

04:00.560 --> 04:03.500
It all comes back to a single ancient Greek word, doesn't it?

04:03.560 --> 04:08.020
It really is one of those linguistic keys that unlocks a whole new way of seeing the world.

04:08.520 --> 04:09.840
The word is kybernetis.

04:10.240 --> 04:10.640
Kybernetis.

04:10.640 --> 04:16.820
Right. In ancient Greek, it means the helmsman or the steersman of a ship, the person standing at the back of the boat holding the tiller.

04:16.920 --> 04:18.520
Okay, so the guy steering the boat.

04:18.980 --> 04:29.580
Exactly. And what's so profound here is that this single root birthed two entirely different, seemingly unrelated concepts that we use all the time today.

04:29.640 --> 04:30.560
Okay, lay it on me.

04:30.980 --> 04:37.140
Well, the Romans took kybernetis and formed the Latin word guberner, which literally means to steer or govern.

04:37.580 --> 04:40.140
Wait, so that is where we get the English word government?

04:40.140 --> 04:49.700
Exactly. But then, centuries later, in 1948, the mathematician Norbert Wiener was trying to formalize a new science.

04:50.080 --> 04:50.960
A science of what?

04:51.200 --> 04:56.000
He was looking at how biological animals and mechanical machines communicate and control themselves.

04:56.600 --> 05:00.040
He needed a word for this new science of feedback loops.

05:00.040 --> 05:02.300
Don't tell me he went back to the Greek word.

05:02.300 --> 05:07.580
He did. He went back to that exact same ancient Greek root and coined the term cybernetics.

05:07.920 --> 05:15.080
Wow. So, government and cybernetics are literally linguistic twins. They come from the exact same idea of steering a ship.

05:15.200 --> 05:15.820
They really do.

05:16.140 --> 05:22.360
And if you take a second to think about what a helmsman actually does in the real world, it changes the entire metaphor of power?

05:22.360 --> 05:26.280
Because a helmsman on a wooden ship in the middle of the ocean doesn't command the ocean.

05:26.620 --> 05:29.500
Right. They can't stand on the deck and yell at a hurricane to calm down.

05:29.840 --> 05:31.880
I mean, they can try, but it won't work.

05:32.020 --> 05:35.920
They can't dictate the ocean currents or pass a law against rogue waves.

05:36.020 --> 05:36.680
So, what do they do?

05:36.820 --> 05:42.920
All a helmsman can do is continually estimate the environment around them, predict where the ship is heading,

05:43.560 --> 05:48.940
and apply limited, tiny control inputs to the rudder to keep the ship from sinking.

05:48.940 --> 05:53.560
That distinction you just made between commanding reality and steering through it,

05:53.680 --> 05:56.600
that seems like the absolute foundation of this entire framework.

05:56.820 --> 06:02.020
It really is. Traditional political science has this terrible habit of looking at society

06:02.020 --> 06:04.120
as a state of static equilibrium.

06:04.460 --> 06:06.780
Like, if we just write the perfect laws, we're done.

06:06.960 --> 06:11.620
Exactly. It assumes that if you just sit down, debate the issues, get the laws right,

06:11.720 --> 06:16.420
and structure the institutions perfectly, you achieve a stable state forever.

06:16.420 --> 06:18.340
It treats society like a photograph.

06:18.940 --> 06:20.800
Once the picture's taken, it's done.

06:21.200 --> 06:25.480
But constitutional cybernetics looks at society as a continuous trajectory.

06:25.820 --> 06:27.960
It's a movie that never stops rolling.

06:28.120 --> 06:29.740
Right. Because things are always changing.

06:30.040 --> 06:34.400
Always. The economy is always mutating. Demographic populations are shifting.

06:35.020 --> 06:36.860
Disruptive technology is advancing.

06:37.240 --> 06:38.520
Unpredictable disturbances.

06:38.740 --> 06:44.140
Yes. Like global pandemics, sudden market crashes, or climate disasters.

06:44.140 --> 06:46.900
They're constantly slamming into the hull of the ship.

06:47.040 --> 06:52.600
So if it's a movie, the government is just constantly running what engineers call the classical cybernetic loop.

06:52.740 --> 06:56.740
Right. The observe, estimate, compare, control loop.

06:57.060 --> 07:00.200
Observe, estimate, compare, control, and then observe again.

07:01.400 --> 07:02.840
I'm picturing the steersman here.

07:02.900 --> 07:03.100
Yeah.

07:03.100 --> 07:06.700
They feel the spray of the ocean in the direction of the wind.

07:06.820 --> 07:07.760
That's observation, right?

07:07.780 --> 07:08.080
Exactly.

07:08.420 --> 07:12.300
Then they take that feeling, and guess how far off course the ship has drifted?

07:12.540 --> 07:13.400
That's estimation.

07:13.560 --> 07:15.040
Yep. They are building a mental model.

07:15.200 --> 07:18.640
Then they look down at the compass to see the heading they're actually supposed to be on.

07:19.020 --> 07:19.760
That's comparison.

07:20.100 --> 07:22.400
Then they use their muscles to turn the wooden wheel.

07:22.640 --> 07:23.420
That's control.

07:23.580 --> 07:24.840
And then they don't just walk away.

07:24.840 --> 07:29.300
They immediately stand there and feel the wind again to see if that turn actually did anything.

07:29.440 --> 07:30.300
It's an endless loop.

07:30.760 --> 07:32.340
That is the exact mechanism.

07:32.980 --> 07:38.720
And Flyxion's argument is that every single thing a government does, no matter how complex or bureaucratic it seems,

07:39.140 --> 07:44.260
is just a specific scaled-up implementation of this exact feedback loop.

07:44.480 --> 07:45.040
Wait, really?

07:45.700 --> 07:46.600
Every single thing?

07:46.780 --> 07:48.120
Every single thing.

07:48.120 --> 07:52.940
Whether you are looking at a central bank committee adjusting national interest rates to cool down inflation,

07:53.240 --> 07:57.560
or a legislature arguing for three months over an infrastructure budget.

07:57.740 --> 08:01.180
Or a Supreme Court reviewing the constitutionality of a new surveillance law.

08:01.280 --> 08:01.580
Yes.

08:01.680 --> 08:05.600
Or even a local environmental agency tracking pollution in a river.

08:06.120 --> 08:10.760
They are all just executing the observe, estimate, compare, control loop.

08:10.960 --> 08:17.760
So the objective of governance isn't to reach some perfect, static, utopian society where everything is solved forever.

08:17.760 --> 08:18.400
Not at all.

08:18.700 --> 08:22.780
The objective is to preserve the system's capacity to keep adapting to the next wave.

08:23.060 --> 08:24.840
Let me see if I can put an analogy on this.

08:24.940 --> 08:27.840
So I want to make sure I'm wrapping my head around this shift in values here.

08:27.940 --> 08:28.440
Go for it.

08:28.720 --> 08:34.540
It seems to me that traditional politics judges a pilot by how shiny their uniform is,

08:34.740 --> 08:36.160
what speeches they give in the terminal,

08:36.700 --> 08:40.500
and maybe by whether the passengers in the cabin voted for them to be in the cockpit.

08:40.960 --> 08:41.320
Sure.

08:41.460 --> 08:43.160
That's the classic view of legitimacy.

08:43.540 --> 08:46.480
But cybernetics doesn't care about the uniform or the speeches.

08:46.480 --> 08:51.460
It judges the pilot purely by whether they can keep the plane in the air

08:51.460 --> 08:54.980
when a Category 5 hurricane suddenly forms right in front of them.

08:55.300 --> 08:57.800
That is entirely brutally functional, yes.

08:57.920 --> 09:00.940
I have to push back a little here because I'm feeling a sense of unease.

09:01.260 --> 09:01.580
Uh-oh.

09:02.020 --> 09:02.500
What's wrong?

09:02.560 --> 09:05.260
Well, isn't this framework a bit, I don't know, cold?

09:05.260 --> 09:08.700
We are talking about human society.

09:09.000 --> 09:11.380
We are talking about laws that put people in prison,

09:11.840 --> 09:14.480
budget debates that determine if children get school lunches,

09:14.620 --> 09:17.040
the messy reality of human lives.

09:17.180 --> 09:17.940
I see where you're going.

09:17.940 --> 09:23.720
And this cybernetic theory seems to reduce all of that passion, morality, and suffering

09:23.720 --> 09:27.160
to an automated thermostat regulating the air conditioning in a house.

09:27.800 --> 09:32.260
It sounds like we are stripping the humanity and the moral weight out of politics entirely.

09:32.660 --> 09:34.240
I completely understand that reaction.

09:34.760 --> 09:39.400
It's usually the very first objection people have when you apply control theory to society.

09:39.660 --> 09:41.880
That it feels deeply technocratic and sterile.

09:41.880 --> 09:42.320
Exactly.

09:42.740 --> 09:45.000
But if we dig a little deeper, it's actually the opposite.

09:45.260 --> 09:51.160
It's not about automating humans or reducing us to mindless cogs in a giant machine.

09:51.360 --> 09:52.400
Okay, then what is it about?

09:52.780 --> 09:59.620
It's about recognizing the severe, unavoidable, and often tragic limitations of human institutions.

10:00.720 --> 10:06.100
A thermostat is a simple controller because it operates in a simple, closed environment.

10:06.340 --> 10:06.520
Right.

10:06.600 --> 10:08.340
A house doesn't change its fundamental nature.

10:08.580 --> 10:09.080
Exactly.

10:09.080 --> 10:11.840
But human societies are infinitely complex.

10:12.000 --> 10:13.140
They are constantly evolving.

10:13.740 --> 10:19.120
The so-called thermostat of government is constantly being overwhelmed by incomplete information,

10:19.400 --> 10:21.260
delayed signals, and human bias.

10:21.560 --> 10:22.000
Oh, I see.

10:22.080 --> 10:26.160
So acknowledging that government is a cybernetic loop isn't a cold dismissal of humanity.

10:26.700 --> 10:29.380
It's a profound plea for epistemic humility.

10:29.600 --> 10:32.200
Meaning we have to admit how little we actually know.

10:32.540 --> 10:32.920
Yes.

10:32.920 --> 10:39.180
It tells us that no leader, no matter how morally righteous their intentions, and no matter how

10:39.180 --> 10:44.500
beautiful their speeches are, can successfully govern if they don't have accurate sensors.

10:44.840 --> 10:48.460
Or if the steering wheel they are holding is completely disconnected from the rudder.

10:48.720 --> 10:49.240
Exactly.

10:49.500 --> 10:54.400
You can have the most moral pilot in the world, but if their dashboard is telling them they are

10:54.400 --> 11:00.240
going up when they are actually going down, they are going to fly the plane straight into

11:00.240 --> 11:00.740
a mountain.

11:01.100 --> 11:03.880
And their good intentions won't save a single passenger.

11:04.300 --> 11:05.460
That's the reality of it.

11:05.500 --> 11:06.420
That makes a lot of sense.

11:06.740 --> 11:11.360
Which leads us to what seems like the most terrifying hurdle the steersman faces.

11:11.940 --> 11:17.700
If government is the helmsman and it relies entirely on its instruments to see the ocean,

11:18.160 --> 11:20.140
how does it actually see?

11:20.280 --> 11:21.340
Well, this is the kicker.

11:21.340 --> 11:25.520
Because reading through the monograph, the terrifying truth seems to be that it can't.

11:25.540 --> 11:26.520
Not directly, anyway.

11:26.680 --> 11:31.060
You're touching on what the text calls the observer problem, which is perhaps the most

11:31.060 --> 11:33.680
humbling concept in the entire theory.

11:33.860 --> 11:34.760
The observer problem.

11:34.860 --> 11:35.720
Unpack that for us.

11:36.000 --> 11:40.840
In our daily lives, we casually talk about the state of the economy or the state of public

11:40.840 --> 11:42.940
health as if they are physical objects.

11:43.200 --> 11:46.380
Like things you can just put on a scale and weigh or measure with a tape measure.

11:46.500 --> 11:46.880
Right.

11:47.040 --> 11:50.600
But the true social state is infinite in its dimensionality.

11:50.600 --> 11:57.800
It is made up of billions of daily interactions, undocumented emotional states, hidden financial

11:57.800 --> 12:01.420
transactions, microscopic biological realities.

12:01.600 --> 12:02.860
So it's just too big to comprehend.

12:03.120 --> 12:03.980
Way too big.

12:04.040 --> 12:11.400
There is no single instrument, no central authority, and no supercomputer on Earth that has direct,

12:11.860 --> 12:15.220
unfettered access to the complete reality of a society.

12:15.500 --> 12:18.100
So the government is essentially always flying blind.

12:18.360 --> 12:18.500
Well.

12:18.600 --> 12:19.760
It never actually looks out the window.

12:19.760 --> 12:23.980
It's flying strictly on instruments, and the instruments are inherently, unavoidably

12:23.980 --> 12:24.420
flawed.

12:24.700 --> 12:25.060
Yikes.

12:25.400 --> 12:30.280
To explain this, the framework leans heavily on the 18th century philosopher Immanuel Kant.

12:30.540 --> 12:32.440
Oh, taking us back to philosophy class.

12:32.560 --> 12:33.220
Just for a second.

12:33.820 --> 12:39.480
Kant made this famous foundational distinction between phenomena, which is reality as we perceive

12:39.480 --> 12:42.740
it, filter it, and represent it to ourselves in things in themselves.

12:42.740 --> 12:48.940
The things in themselves being reality as it actually exists in the universe, completely independent

12:48.940 --> 12:50.400
of our ability to observe it.

12:50.480 --> 12:50.960
Exactly.

12:51.560 --> 12:57.100
And Flyxion takes Kant's philosophy and applies it directly to political science.

12:57.460 --> 13:00.300
The government never acts on reality in itself.

13:00.520 --> 13:02.500
It is mathematically impossible.

13:02.500 --> 13:04.080
It only ever acts on phenomena.

13:04.080 --> 13:04.480
Yes.

13:04.480 --> 13:09.860
It acts on an estimated internal state that it has reconstructed from delayed, noisy, and

13:09.860 --> 13:11.920
often totally contradictory observations.

13:12.280 --> 13:17.360
I want to make sure we don't lose anyone here, because there is a mathematical formula in the text that explains this.

13:17.880 --> 13:21.720
And honestly, when I first saw the Greek letters, my eyes totally glazed over.

13:21.720 --> 13:23.220
Yeah, formulas can do that.

13:23.280 --> 13:25.820
But once I sat with it, it became incredibly profound.

13:26.660 --> 13:30.500
The formula is AT, high ET, plus AT.

13:30.860 --> 13:32.860
It looks intimidating, but it's brilliant.

13:33.160 --> 13:34.260
Let's not just read the math.

13:34.340 --> 13:35.200
Let's ground this.

13:35.620 --> 13:36.540
Let's build a scenario.

13:36.980 --> 13:40.160
Imagine a new, mysterious virus starts spreading through a country.

13:40.660 --> 13:43.820
How does this formula explain what the government actually sees?

13:44.080 --> 13:46.100
That's a perfect scenario to break this down.

13:46.800 --> 13:47.580
Let's look at the pieces.

13:47.580 --> 13:54.300
In your pandemic scenario, represents the true state of society at that exact moment in time.

13:54.420 --> 13:55.140
The thing in itself.

13:55.360 --> 13:55.560
Right.

13:55.720 --> 13:59.360
It's the actual, precise number of people who have the virus.

13:59.700 --> 14:02.220
Exactly how the virus is mutating in their bodies.

14:02.520 --> 14:04.960
The exact number of hospital beds available.

14:05.560 --> 14:08.660
The exact economic impact of people staying home.

14:08.860 --> 14:14.340
Basically, an infinitely complex reality that the government cannot ever perfectly know.

14:14.560 --> 14:14.820
Right.

14:14.940 --> 14:16.860
God knows, X and A, but the president doesn't.

14:16.860 --> 14:19.980
Okay, so the president doesn't have a direct line to six and eighters.

14:20.120 --> 14:24.640
Instead, the government relies on A of dollars, which is the specific lens or the measurement

14:24.640 --> 14:26.540
function of a particular observer.

14:26.860 --> 14:29.520
Okay, give me an example of an observer in this pandemic.

14:29.900 --> 14:33.660
Let's say HA1 is a rural hospital's testing capacity.

14:34.500 --> 14:38.100
Tudotru 2 might be a network of epidemiologists looking at wastewater.

14:38.900 --> 14:43.400
Tudotru 3s is an economist looking at credit card spending data to see if people are going

14:43.400 --> 14:44.060
to restaurants.

14:44.060 --> 14:48.540
Each of these observers is trying to look at 16, but their lens is incredibly narrow.

14:48.780 --> 14:49.040
Yes.

14:49.260 --> 14:54.480
They can only see the slice of reality that their specific tools allow them to see.

14:54.820 --> 14:58.920
And then we get to the really dangerous part of the formula, the card's P.

14:59.600 --> 15:01.180
This represents the noise, right?

15:01.260 --> 15:01.480
Yes.

15:01.840 --> 15:02.780
Tight is the distortion.

15:03.100 --> 15:05.240
It's the unavoidable noise in the signal.

15:05.440 --> 15:06.160
What kind of noise?

15:06.160 --> 15:10.960
Well, for the rural hospital, the noise might be a two-week delay in getting test results

15:10.960 --> 15:11.820
back from the lab.

15:12.140 --> 15:16.680
For the epidemiologists, the noise might be a faulty chemical region that gives false

15:16.680 --> 15:17.240
positives.

15:17.580 --> 15:19.340
So mechanical or scientific noise?

15:19.680 --> 15:20.120
Exactly.

15:20.380 --> 15:21.600
But noise isn't just mechanical.

15:21.840 --> 15:23.020
It can be political, too.

15:23.320 --> 15:23.940
Oh, like what?

15:24.100 --> 15:29.420
If a local mayor wants to look good for re-election, they might pressure the hospital to undercount

15:29.420 --> 15:29.980
the deaths.

15:30.200 --> 15:32.080
That political pressure is Thai.

15:32.340 --> 15:33.500
It distorts the measurement.

15:33.500 --> 15:33.980
Wow.

15:34.520 --> 15:38.720
So when the output finally reaches the central government, what they get is Thai.

15:39.220 --> 15:39.580
Correct.

15:39.820 --> 15:41.860
They don't get the true reality of the pandemic.

15:41.860 --> 15:48.060
They just get one tiny, delayed, politically distorted, scientifically narrow slice of data.

15:48.360 --> 15:52.920
And when the government decides to issue a massive society-wide lockdown or a vaccine

15:52.920 --> 15:57.640
mandate, which is a huge control action, it's not basing it on the true reality.

15:57.640 --> 16:06.460
It's basing it on a massive, messy, patched-together amalgamation of millions of these flawed nidicals.

16:06.460 --> 16:06.960
Precisely.

16:07.060 --> 16:10.700
The government is always trying to reconstruct a map of a territory it can never actually

16:10.700 --> 16:11.080
visit.

16:11.260 --> 16:12.160
That is wild.

16:12.280 --> 16:17.400
And because every formal system is incomplete, the text actually draws on Kurt Gödel's

16:17.400 --> 16:21.580
incompleteness theorems here to show that no system can perfectly verify itself from

16:21.580 --> 16:22.140
the inside.

16:22.140 --> 16:26.900
There is always, always a gap between the map and the territory.

16:27.580 --> 16:32.160
So governing is basically an inherently recursive process of continual approximation.

16:32.760 --> 16:37.080
You gather the messy data, you make a best guess, you steer the ship, you check the noisy

16:37.080 --> 16:37.880
instruments again.

16:38.020 --> 16:40.860
You realize your guess was slightly wrong and you oversteered.

16:41.000 --> 16:41.140
Yeah.

16:41.200 --> 16:42.200
And you try to correct it.

16:42.300 --> 16:42.600
Exactly.

16:42.740 --> 16:43.600
Round and round forever.

16:43.940 --> 16:45.480
I am synthesizing this.

16:45.580 --> 16:50.140
And here's where it gets incredibly exciting for me, because this totally changes how we argue

16:50.140 --> 16:50.960
about civil liberties.

16:50.960 --> 16:51.840
Oh, big time.

16:52.460 --> 16:58.780
If the government entirely relies on this distributed, decentralized network of censors to have any

16:58.780 --> 17:04.520
clue what is going on, then things like freedom of the press, academic inquiry, and civil society

17:04.520 --> 17:07.100
aren't just polite moral ideals.

17:07.400 --> 17:11.860
No, they are absolute non-negotiable engineering necessities.

17:12.220 --> 17:17.900
I think this is one of the most profound, world-shifting takeaways from Flipchon's work.

17:17.900 --> 17:23.100
Because in our traditional political discourse, we usually defend free speech by saying it's

17:23.100 --> 17:24.380
a fundamental human right.

17:24.780 --> 17:29.060
Or we quote John Stuart Mill and say it's vital for human flourishing and the marketplace

17:29.060 --> 17:29.860
of ideas.

17:30.220 --> 17:31.780
And it absolutely is.

17:31.900 --> 17:34.060
But from a purely cybernetic perspective.

17:34.140 --> 17:37.680
From a cybernetic perspective, free speech is an observability condition.

17:37.880 --> 17:41.000
Meaning if you don't have it, you can't observe the state.

17:41.000 --> 17:41.600
Exactly.

17:41.600 --> 17:47.520
If a government suppresses independent journalists, or if it defunds scientific research it doesn't

17:47.520 --> 17:52.660
like, or if it silences political opposition, it is mathematically reducing the dimensionality

17:52.660 --> 17:54.700
of its own control system's brain.

17:54.700 --> 17:56.540
Let's go back to our airplane pilot.

17:56.660 --> 17:58.400
It's like a pilot who is flying through a storm.

17:59.040 --> 18:03.220
They look down at the altimeter, and the altimeter says they are losing altitude rapidly.

18:03.420 --> 18:05.560
And the pilot doesn't like what the altimeter is saying.

18:05.720 --> 18:06.760
It makes them feel anxious.

18:07.280 --> 18:12.620
So they take a hammer and smash the glass, and then they turn around and smash the fuel

18:12.620 --> 18:17.860
gauge, because they've decided the fuel gauge is spreading fake news about the plane being

18:17.860 --> 18:18.760
low on gas.

18:19.060 --> 18:21.100
Which is obviously a terrible idea.

18:21.100 --> 18:25.600
Smashing the instruments might make the pilot feel incredibly powerful and secure for about

18:25.600 --> 18:28.680
10 minutes, but it is mathematically suicidal.

18:28.780 --> 18:30.640
Because the plane is still running out of gas.

18:30.880 --> 18:32.380
It is still falling out of the sky.

18:32.640 --> 18:35.320
The pilot just won't see the mountain coming until they crash into it.

18:35.520 --> 18:39.240
That analogy perfectly captures the mechanics of authoritarianism.

18:39.980 --> 18:46.760
Censorship, state propaganda, and institutional secrecy literally reduce the rank of the observation

18:46.760 --> 18:47.300
operator.

18:47.300 --> 18:51.000
The central controller, meaning the government, continues to act, of course.

18:51.100 --> 18:56.820
It keeps passing laws and deploying police, but its internal estimate of reality rapidly

18:56.820 --> 18:58.860
diverges from actual reality.

18:58.860 --> 19:01.620
The control actions become completely maladaptive.

19:01.980 --> 19:06.200
They start solving problems that don't exist and ignoring crises that are actually tearing

19:06.200 --> 19:07.180
the society apart.

19:07.680 --> 19:13.580
A government that destroys its distributed observer network will eventually destabilize, regardless

19:13.580 --> 19:19.280
of how many tanks it has or how brutal its police force is, simply because it has intentionally

19:19.280 --> 19:20.320
blinded itself.

19:20.320 --> 19:25.160
So an open society isn't just morally superior, it is mathematically more robust because it

19:25.160 --> 19:27.220
has more active sensors gathering data.

19:28.040 --> 19:31.680
But that introduces a massive new headache, doesn't it?

19:31.760 --> 19:32.520
It really does.

19:32.760 --> 19:35.160
Let's say a society is doing great on human rights.

19:35.660 --> 19:38.800
It has a thriving, completely free network of sensors.

19:39.220 --> 19:40.140
We have economists.

19:40.500 --> 19:41.420
We have everyday citizens.

19:41.600 --> 19:42.160
We have doctors.

19:42.340 --> 19:43.080
We have urban planners.

19:43.080 --> 19:46.640
All constantly gathering data and shouting it up to the helmsman.

19:46.700 --> 19:47.720
Sounds great on paper.

19:47.920 --> 19:50.800
But what happens when none of those sensors speak the same language?

19:50.800 --> 19:55.980
This is where we run into the limits of just gathering data, and it introduces what the

19:55.980 --> 19:57.880
monograph calls the Babel Protocol.

19:58.320 --> 19:59.460
The Babel Protocol.

19:59.460 --> 20:01.140
That sounds very dramatic.

20:01.140 --> 20:04.640
Well, we aren't talking about simple linguistic translation here.

20:04.740 --> 20:08.860
It's not just about someone speaking English and someone else speaking Mandarin, where you

20:08.860 --> 20:10.940
just need a dictionary to swap the words.

20:11.260 --> 20:12.640
Okay, what kind of translation is it?

20:12.820 --> 20:18.860
The Babel Protocol is dealing with entirely incompatible representational frameworks, or what the text

20:18.860 --> 20:22.300
mathematically refers to as semantic manifolds.

20:22.660 --> 20:23.640
Semantic manifolds.

20:23.640 --> 20:29.100
I think I need an example of a semantic manifold, because this sounds like we are all living in

20:29.100 --> 20:29.860
different realities.

20:30.100 --> 20:30.880
We kind of are.

20:31.080 --> 20:31.700
Let me try this.

20:32.540 --> 20:35.060
An economist looks at a period of high inflation.

20:35.660 --> 20:36.380
They pull up a chart.

20:37.120 --> 20:41.800
Their semantic manifold is made of numbers, money supply curves, and interest rate adjustments.

20:42.620 --> 20:46.940
They see inflation as a macroeconomic variable that needs a 2% adjustment.

20:47.120 --> 20:47.940
Perfect example.

20:48.100 --> 20:52.340
But a citizen who just walked out of a grocery store doesn't see a macroeconomic chart.

20:52.340 --> 20:54.060
They don't experience a 2% variable.

20:54.060 --> 20:58.620
No, their semantic manifold is a narrative of their purchasing power disappearing.

20:59.260 --> 21:02.740
They experience visceral anxiety about feeding their children.

21:03.060 --> 21:03.300
Exactly.

21:03.640 --> 21:09.200
Or, like, a doctor looking at a pandemic sees biological viral loads and spike proteins,

21:09.460 --> 21:14.000
while an architect looking at the exact same pandemic sees building ventilation systems

21:14.000 --> 21:15.060
and airflow constraints.

21:15.900 --> 21:17.380
Are those semantic manifolds?

21:17.760 --> 21:18.860
They absolutely are.

21:18.940 --> 21:22.220
These different observers don't just possess different vocabularies.

21:22.340 --> 21:25.260
They possess entirely different ontologies.

21:25.560 --> 21:29.820
Different ontologies, meaning they categorize reality in fundamentally different ways.

21:29.940 --> 21:30.320
Exactly.

21:30.720 --> 21:33.600
The architect isn't just using different words than the doctor.

21:33.940 --> 21:36.820
They are measuring completely different properties of the universe.

21:37.520 --> 21:39.480
So how does the Babel Protocol fix this?

21:39.760 --> 21:45.060
Well, the Babel Protocol is the theoretical architecture required for a government to translate

21:45.060 --> 21:50.940
between these spaces, but it's incredibly difficult because it's not a literal dictionary you can

21:50.940 --> 21:51.600
just look up.

21:51.660 --> 21:54.200
There's no Google Translate for semantic manifold.

21:54.360 --> 21:54.560
Nope.

21:55.060 --> 21:59.860
The text actually brings up some brilliant sci-fi examples to illustrate how complex this is,

21:59.980 --> 22:03.800
like the Babel Fish from Douglas Adams' The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy,

22:03.800 --> 22:06.320
or the aliens in the movie Arrival.

22:06.700 --> 22:09.420
Oh, Arrival is the perfect cultural touchstone for this.

22:09.520 --> 22:10.260
It really is.

22:10.260 --> 22:14.540
In that movie, without spoiling too much, the challenge wasn't just pointing to a tree

22:14.540 --> 22:16.640
and learning what alien sound meant, tree.

22:17.440 --> 22:22.900
The aliens, the heptapods, experienced the flow of time in a completely non-linear way.

22:23.100 --> 22:23.400
Right.

22:23.620 --> 22:26.080
They saw the past, present, and future simultaneously.

22:26.080 --> 22:32.320
Their entire conceptual geometry, their semantic manifold, was fundamentally alien.

22:32.900 --> 22:36.700
To actually translate their language and communicate with them, the human linguist,

22:36.820 --> 22:41.940
played by Amy Adams, had to literally rewire the neural pathways in her own brain

22:41.940 --> 22:44.540
to understand their geometry of time.

22:44.680 --> 22:46.040
She couldn't just learn their words.

22:46.160 --> 22:47.640
She had to learn their reality.

22:47.900 --> 22:48.140
Exactly.

22:48.300 --> 22:49.360
And that's exactly it.

22:49.360 --> 22:53.400
A true, universal translator, if one could even exist,

22:53.840 --> 22:56.900
wouldn't just be an algorithm that swaps English for heptapod.

22:57.320 --> 23:00.000
It would have to account for the entire state of the observer.

23:00.260 --> 23:01.300
Meaning what, exactly?

23:01.380 --> 23:03.900
It would have to know who is speaking, who is listening,

23:04.420 --> 23:08.520
their deep historical context, their unstated cultural assumptions,

23:09.180 --> 23:12.900
their current emotional state, and the structural limitations of their brain.

23:13.400 --> 23:15.060
Meaning, does not live in a vacuum.

23:15.240 --> 23:16.620
It doesn't just float around in the air?

23:16.620 --> 23:19.920
No, meaning lives in the entire state of the observer.

23:20.460 --> 23:23.420
So when we talk about the Babel Protocol in government,

23:23.840 --> 23:29.360
we are talking about the ongoing, incredibly difficult, and deeply imperfect process

23:29.360 --> 23:35.560
of creating coordinate transformations between these radically different conceptual spaces

23:35.560 --> 23:37.660
within a single society.

23:37.960 --> 23:41.920
The monograph uses this phrase, language is deictic control.

23:42.140 --> 23:42.520
Yes.

23:42.580 --> 23:43.600
If I'm understanding that right.

23:43.600 --> 23:48.240
It basically means we don't use language to perfectly describe absolute truth.

23:48.560 --> 23:52.480
We use language to create temporary shared coordinate systems,

23:52.600 --> 23:55.980
just so we can solve a specific problem together.

23:56.520 --> 23:59.000
It's like setting up temporary scaffolding on the side of a building.

23:59.840 --> 24:02.740
We don't live on the scaffolding, but we need it to fix the window.

24:02.900 --> 24:04.200
That's a great way to visualize it.

24:04.420 --> 24:09.020
And this realization completely redefines how we should look at political gridlock.

24:09.160 --> 24:09.960
Oh, how so?

24:09.960 --> 24:13.540
Well, we look at a paralyzed legislature, say the U.S. Congress,

24:13.940 --> 24:17.720
and we usually assume the gridlock is a clash of fundamental moral values,

24:17.920 --> 24:19.840
or just petty partisan stubbornness.

24:20.040 --> 24:24.160
We think they're looking at the same problem and just refusing to agree on a solution.

24:24.380 --> 24:26.200
That's definitely what it looks like on cable news.

24:26.440 --> 24:30.740
But from a cybernetic view, much of what we call political gridlock

24:30.740 --> 24:35.280
is actually a catastrophic, epistemic failure of the Babel Protocol.

24:35.280 --> 24:39.840
The participants are arguing over completely different projections of reality

24:39.840 --> 24:41.820
using incompatible geometries.

24:42.180 --> 24:44.200
So they aren't disagreeing on the solution to the problem.

24:44.320 --> 24:46.640
They are disagreeing on what the problem actually is,

24:46.700 --> 24:49.740
because their maps of reality don't overlap at all.

24:49.880 --> 24:50.300
Exactly.

24:50.480 --> 24:52.540
Let's say they are debating a housing crisis.

24:53.380 --> 24:57.620
A developer's map says the problem is zoning regulations stopping supply.

24:58.140 --> 25:02.160
A local tenant's map says the problem is predatory corporate landlords.

25:02.160 --> 25:07.480
An environmentalist's map says the problem is urban sprawl destroying wetlands.

25:07.880 --> 25:09.740
And they are all experiencing the housing crisis,

25:10.080 --> 25:12.940
but they are trying to shout instructions to the helmsman

25:12.940 --> 25:15.200
using completely different coordinate systems.

25:15.480 --> 25:19.360
But this raises a really daunting question for you, the listener, and for me.

25:20.060 --> 25:23.560
If we are all operating in these different semantic coordinate systems,

25:23.800 --> 25:28.640
if the lawyer and the scientist and the citizen literally categorize reality differently,

25:28.640 --> 25:32.220
how do we ever agree on what the actual state of the world is?

25:32.320 --> 25:33.500
It's a huge challenge.

25:33.860 --> 25:38.360
Don't we just end up talking past each other forever until the system collapses?

25:38.740 --> 25:43.680
We absolutely would if we demanded perfect, permanent, conceptual uniformity.

25:43.940 --> 25:47.160
If we demanded that everyone see the world exactly the same way,

25:47.520 --> 25:49.100
society would fracture instantly.

25:49.360 --> 25:49.660
Right.

25:50.020 --> 25:53.180
But the Babel Protocol isn't about making everyone think the same way.

25:53.280 --> 25:56.420
It's about achieving semantic interoperability.

25:56.620 --> 25:57.820
Semantic interoperability.

25:57.820 --> 26:01.900
You don't need the citizen to become a trained macroeconomist,

26:01.940 --> 26:04.460
and you don't need the environmental lawyer to become an architect.

26:04.740 --> 26:08.900
You just need to build a temporary bridge, a shared estimation space,

26:09.100 --> 26:13.680
where the citizen's lived experience of poverty can be translated into data

26:13.680 --> 26:16.160
the economist can actually plug into their model.

26:16.520 --> 26:19.120
And the economist model can be translated into a policy

26:19.120 --> 26:21.300
that actually relieves the citizen's anxiety.

26:21.700 --> 26:22.000
Yes.

26:22.000 --> 26:27.400
It's a constant, messy, exhausting, ongoing negotiation of temporary standards.

26:27.820 --> 26:33.920
When that negotiation fails, the distributed estimation network fragments into isolated echo chambers.

26:34.080 --> 26:37.700
And the central government entirely loses the ability to act coherently.

26:37.840 --> 26:38.240
Precisely.

26:38.240 --> 26:43.840
Okay, so before we can steer the ship, we have to agree on a temporary map that we can all read.

26:44.320 --> 26:49.020
But in human society, the government isn't just reading a map that was handed to it by God.

26:49.420 --> 26:52.620
The government is drawing the map while it sails the ship.

26:52.800 --> 26:53.060
Right.

26:53.060 --> 26:58.320
Which takes us into how the government decides what is even worth measuring in the first place.

26:58.320 --> 27:01.320
This gets into the deep epistemology of government.

27:01.820 --> 27:04.580
We just talked about how different observers use different maps,

27:04.820 --> 27:09.060
but who decides what goes on the official map that the central controller uses?

27:09.320 --> 27:09.460
Right.

27:10.040 --> 27:12.540
Flyxion points out that the variables a government tracks,

27:12.660 --> 27:16.640
things like unemployment, inflation, mental illness, or poverty,

27:16.640 --> 27:20.460
are not natural facts just waiting out in the wild to be discovered,

27:20.740 --> 27:24.160
like a new species of bird or a rock formation.

27:24.280 --> 27:25.980
They are representational constructs.

27:26.020 --> 27:27.440
They are invented categories.

27:27.600 --> 27:30.380
The text cites the friend philosopher Michel Foucault here,

27:30.760 --> 27:32.960
specifically his history of psychiatry.

27:32.960 --> 27:34.660
Which I think is a brilliant connection.

27:35.660 --> 27:39.120
Foucault argued that the way we classify madness or mental illness

27:39.120 --> 27:43.140
isn't just a purely objective, neutral scientific discovery.

27:43.680 --> 27:47.620
The category of mental illness was created by human institutions.

27:47.880 --> 27:51.220
By the medical establishment, the legal system, public administration.

27:51.660 --> 27:51.860
Right.

27:52.220 --> 27:54.200
And once you invent a category like that,

27:54.260 --> 27:55.940
and once you put it on the official map,

27:56.300 --> 27:59.640
it completely alters the cybernetic control loop of society.

27:59.880 --> 28:02.480
You start building specialized asylums and hospitals.

28:02.860 --> 28:05.020
You pass laws about who can be committed.

28:05.500 --> 28:07.520
You redirect billions of dollars in funding.

28:07.520 --> 28:10.060
The category creates a new reality.

28:10.380 --> 28:12.120
Let's look at an even more universal example.

28:12.820 --> 28:13.300
Unemployment.

28:13.440 --> 28:14.160
That's a great one.

28:14.260 --> 28:16.560
Before the late 19th and early 20th centuries,

28:17.080 --> 28:22.580
the concept of unemployment as a standardized, measurable, statistical category

28:22.580 --> 28:25.220
didn't really exist in the way we think of it today.

28:25.360 --> 28:28.740
People were poor, or they were itinerant, or they were idle,

28:29.000 --> 28:32.940
but the government didn't have a monthly unemployment rate dashboard on CNN.

28:33.420 --> 28:35.960
Because it wasn't formalized as a state variable,

28:35.960 --> 28:37.920
governments didn't try to control it.

28:38.320 --> 28:42.640
If you were out of work, it was a local, moral failing, or just bad luck.

28:42.640 --> 28:45.880
But once the government formalized the category of unemployment,

28:46.800 --> 28:50.440
it fundamentally changed the state space of governance.

28:50.980 --> 28:52.280
It became a target for policy?

28:52.280 --> 28:52.760
Yes.

28:53.320 --> 28:55.840
The government began tracking it, estimating it,

28:55.960 --> 29:00.000
and passing sweeping macroeconomic controls to manipulate it.

29:00.560 --> 29:04.180
The government is continually constructing the coordinate system

29:04.180 --> 29:06.560
through which society becomes observable.

29:06.780 --> 29:09.580
So, we build the map, we invent the categories,

29:09.780 --> 29:11.220
and we gather the messy data.

29:11.620 --> 29:12.440
We turn the wheel.

29:12.980 --> 29:15.940
But how do we know if our steering is actually working?

29:16.400 --> 29:19.900
How do we measure the actual strength or capacity of the government

29:19.900 --> 29:21.140
to act in a crisis?

29:21.140 --> 29:23.800
This is where we get to fiscal reachability.

29:24.000 --> 29:24.200
Yes.

29:24.500 --> 29:27.380
This is where I encountered the concept of fiscal reachability,

29:27.540 --> 29:30.220
and it completely blew up my understanding of economics.

29:30.480 --> 29:30.860
I agree.

29:30.960 --> 29:33.040
It is a totally paradigm-shifting concept.

29:33.340 --> 29:36.040
Traditional economics usually evaluates the health of a government

29:36.040 --> 29:38.800
by looking at isolated, instantaneous states.

29:39.060 --> 29:41.300
Like, a pundit will go on television and ask,

29:41.660 --> 29:43.060
what is the current budget deficit?

29:43.440 --> 29:46.380
What is the national debt-to-GDP ratio right this second?

29:46.680 --> 29:48.120
What is the inflation rate this month?

29:48.120 --> 29:49.300
They look at a snapshot.

29:50.200 --> 29:53.180
But control theory tells us that looking at a single point in time

29:53.180 --> 29:57.200
is essentially useless for understanding the resilience of a dynamic system.

29:57.200 --> 29:58.740
So, what should we be looking at?

29:59.140 --> 30:02.340
You have to look at the volume of future states a government can reach

30:02.340 --> 30:04.480
without exhausting its control authority.

30:05.100 --> 30:08.900
That mathematical volume of possibilities is fiscal reachability.

30:08.900 --> 30:10.900
Let me bring back the airplane analogy,

30:11.100 --> 30:14.100
because when I mapped fiscal reachability onto aviation,

30:14.720 --> 30:16.240
it instantly clicked for me.

30:16.360 --> 30:16.980
Let's hear it.

30:17.360 --> 30:22.320
Imagine two passenger airplanes flying side-by-side at 1,000 feet,

30:22.880 --> 30:25.740
both traveling at exactly 500 miles an hour.

30:26.460 --> 30:28.940
If you just look at their isolated state,

30:29.420 --> 30:30.780
their altitude, and their speed,

30:31.220 --> 30:32.000
they look identical.

30:32.220 --> 30:33.280
They're perfectly matched.

30:33.340 --> 30:33.580
Right.

30:33.580 --> 30:36.920
This is like looking at two nations that both have a GDP of $2 trillion

30:36.920 --> 30:39.720
and a debt-to-GDP ratio of 80%.

30:39.720 --> 30:41.280
On paper, they are identical.

30:41.420 --> 30:41.760
Exactly.

30:42.200 --> 30:43.600
But, if you look closer,

30:44.140 --> 30:44.820
under the hood,

30:45.240 --> 30:47.400
plane A has completely full fuel tanks,

30:47.760 --> 30:48.780
a well-rested crew,

30:49.260 --> 30:50.600
fully functioning hydraulics,

30:50.760 --> 30:52.420
and strong structural integrity.

30:52.800 --> 30:53.620
Plane B, however,

30:53.820 --> 30:54.980
is running on fumes,

30:55.440 --> 30:56.560
the flaps are jammed,

30:56.800 --> 30:58.260
the co-pilot is exhausted,

30:58.260 --> 31:01.440
and there's a slow-burning electrical fire in the cargo hold.

31:01.680 --> 31:02.020
Yikes.

31:02.180 --> 31:05.640
Plane B might be cruising comfortably at 30,000 feet right now,

31:05.760 --> 31:11.040
but its reachable set of future trajectories is basically just straight down.

31:11.400 --> 31:13.720
Plane A has a massive reachable set.

31:13.860 --> 31:17.060
It can decide to fly to Paris or Tokyo or New York.

31:17.180 --> 31:18.940
It can climb to avoid a storm.

31:19.120 --> 31:21.740
While plane B has exhausted its control authority,

31:22.100 --> 31:24.060
it is fundamentally crashing,

31:24.360 --> 31:26.220
even though the altitude gauge hasn't moved yet.

31:26.400 --> 31:28.000
That is precisely the difference.

31:28.000 --> 31:30.920
Plane B is experiencing actuator saturation.

31:31.260 --> 31:33.780
Its steering wheel no longer controls the rudder.

31:34.460 --> 31:35.940
So, when we evaluate a government,

31:36.080 --> 31:37.760
we shouldn't just look at a spreadsheet and ask,

31:37.860 --> 31:39.020
is the budget balanced today?

31:39.100 --> 31:39.900
We should be asking,

31:40.420 --> 31:42.380
how many admissible future trajectories

31:42.380 --> 31:44.440
does this government still have access to?

31:44.760 --> 31:47.240
Basically, what are our options if things go wrong?

31:47.360 --> 31:47.740
Exactly.

31:47.920 --> 31:50.220
If a massive, unpredictable crisis hits tomorrow,

31:50.560 --> 31:52.440
a new pandemic, a global war,

31:52.860 --> 31:54.820
a catastrophic financial collapse,

31:55.340 --> 31:57.740
does this government have the administrative capacity

31:57.740 --> 31:58.500
to respond?

31:58.500 --> 32:01.220
Does it have the public trust required

32:01.220 --> 32:03.520
to ask citizens to make sacrifices?

32:03.520 --> 32:06.800
Does it have the borrowing power in international markets?

32:07.120 --> 32:09.920
Does it have the legal flexibility to maneuver?

32:10.600 --> 32:11.800
Or is it like Plane B,

32:12.100 --> 32:15.100
where every resource is already tapped out

32:15.100 --> 32:17.760
just to maintain the illusion of level flight?

32:17.760 --> 32:20.380
This totally flips the traditional political debate

32:20.380 --> 32:22.640
on austerity versus government spending.

32:23.140 --> 32:25.360
I feel like we've been having the wrong argument for decades.

32:25.540 --> 32:26.220
We really have.

32:26.580 --> 32:27.860
Austerity cutting budgets,

32:28.340 --> 32:30.340
slashing services to balance the books,

32:30.540 --> 32:33.020
is usually framed in political speeches

32:33.020 --> 32:34.540
as a moral virtue.

32:35.020 --> 32:37.540
It's talked about like a household tightening its belt

32:37.540 --> 32:38.360
to be responsible.

32:38.600 --> 32:39.300
And on the flip side,

32:39.460 --> 32:40.680
strategic government borrowing

32:40.680 --> 32:42.500
is framed as an economic stimulus,

32:42.840 --> 32:44.200
putting money in people's pockets.

32:44.200 --> 32:46.740
But under the lens of constitutional cybernetics,

32:47.080 --> 32:48.680
neither of these are moral choices.

32:49.440 --> 32:51.320
They are purely mathematical maneuvers

32:51.320 --> 32:53.440
to either expand or preserve

32:53.440 --> 32:55.280
future admissible trajectories.

32:55.400 --> 32:56.020
Yes, exactly.

32:56.060 --> 32:58.620
If a government enforces brutal austerity,

32:58.980 --> 33:00.080
and in the process,

33:00.340 --> 33:02.000
they destroy their physical infrastructure,

33:02.560 --> 33:03.800
let their bridges collapse,

33:04.180 --> 33:05.660
and gut their education system,

33:05.960 --> 33:07.500
they are drastically shrinking

33:07.500 --> 33:09.140
their future reachable states.

33:09.440 --> 33:11.400
Because a population that isn't educated

33:11.400 --> 33:13.460
can't pivot to a new tech economy.

33:13.940 --> 33:16.040
They might have a beautifully balanced budget

33:16.040 --> 33:17.080
and zero debt,

33:17.180 --> 33:19.120
but their future options are gone.

33:19.500 --> 33:20.060
Cardversely,

33:20.400 --> 33:22.620
if a government borrows a massive amount of money

33:22.620 --> 33:23.760
to build resilient,

33:24.240 --> 33:25.640
next-generation infrastructure

33:25.640 --> 33:26.980
and green energy grids,

33:27.220 --> 33:28.560
they might look irresponsible

33:28.560 --> 33:29.860
on today's balance sheet.

33:29.960 --> 33:31.560
But they are massively expanding

33:31.560 --> 33:33.140
their future maneuverability

33:33.140 --> 33:34.600
when climate shocks hit.

33:34.600 --> 33:35.860
You've perfectly captured

33:35.860 --> 33:37.820
the cybernetic view of fiscal policy.

33:38.320 --> 33:39.260
A government collapses

33:39.260 --> 33:41.440
when its reachable set contracts to zero.

33:42.000 --> 33:43.540
It simply runs out of options.

33:43.860 --> 33:44.420
It doesn't matter

33:44.420 --> 33:46.120
if its current economic indicators

33:46.120 --> 33:48.080
look fine to the pundits on TV.

33:48.680 --> 33:50.240
If every resource is tapped out,

33:50.340 --> 33:52.260
if public trust is completely eroded,

33:52.660 --> 33:54.380
and if institutional capability

33:54.380 --> 33:55.380
has rusted away,

33:55.740 --> 33:57.460
the slightest external disturbance

33:57.460 --> 33:58.460
will push the system

33:58.460 --> 34:00.140
outside the admissible manifold

34:00.140 --> 34:01.560
and the society will fracture.

34:01.900 --> 34:03.520
Which brings us to the ultimate

34:03.520 --> 34:05.220
structural backstop

34:05.220 --> 34:06.540
of this entire system.

34:06.540 --> 34:08.960
How do we prevent the helmsman

34:08.960 --> 34:11.120
from intentionally or accidentally

34:11.120 --> 34:13.040
driving us into a state

34:13.040 --> 34:14.400
of zero options?

34:14.700 --> 34:14.820
Right.

34:15.080 --> 34:15.940
Because if the government

34:15.940 --> 34:17.100
is this massive,

34:17.600 --> 34:18.940
powerful control loop,

34:19.560 --> 34:20.760
constantly steering,

34:20.980 --> 34:22.680
reallocating billions of dollars

34:22.680 --> 34:24.640
and constructing the map of reality,

34:25.100 --> 34:27.540
what stops it from overcorrecting?

34:27.880 --> 34:29.540
What stops a panicked helmsman

34:29.540 --> 34:30.840
from spinning the wheel

34:30.840 --> 34:32.340
so hard and so fast

34:32.340 --> 34:33.460
that they rip the rudder

34:33.460 --> 34:34.220
right off the ship

34:34.220 --> 34:35.180
and drown everyone?

34:35.180 --> 34:36.660
In physical control engineering,

34:36.880 --> 34:38.040
every system has strict,

34:38.240 --> 34:39.760
unforgiving operational limits.

34:40.360 --> 34:41.260
An airplane has

34:41.260 --> 34:42.220
structural load limits.

34:42.600 --> 34:43.780
You can pull back on the yoke

34:43.780 --> 34:44.600
as hard as you want,

34:44.680 --> 34:46.100
but if you pull too many Gs,

34:46.220 --> 34:47.040
the physical wings

34:47.040 --> 34:49.140
will simply snap off the fuselage.

34:49.180 --> 34:50.060
And a nuclear reactor

34:50.060 --> 34:51.080
has thermal limits.

34:51.300 --> 34:52.160
Push it too hot,

34:52.740 --> 34:53.720
and it melts down.

34:53.900 --> 34:54.860
These limits aren't goals

34:54.860 --> 34:56.080
that the system is trying to achieve.

34:56.200 --> 34:57.800
They are invariant constraints.

34:58.340 --> 34:59.180
You can fly the plane

34:59.180 --> 35:00.160
anywhere you want

35:00.160 --> 35:01.300
as long as you don't exceed

35:01.300 --> 35:02.200
the structural limits

35:02.200 --> 35:02.900
of the airframe.

35:02.900 --> 35:04.380
Flyxion proposes

35:04.380 --> 35:05.600
a radical idea here.

35:05.760 --> 35:07.200
A constitution is the exact

35:07.200 --> 35:08.480
same mathematical object

35:08.480 --> 35:09.640
for a human society.

35:09.640 --> 35:11.740
So a constitution isn't just

35:11.740 --> 35:13.820
a sacred historical document

35:13.820 --> 35:14.800
written on parchment

35:14.800 --> 35:15.660
by our ancestors.

35:15.880 --> 35:17.420
It's not just a social contract.

35:17.860 --> 35:18.520
In this theory,

35:18.660 --> 35:20.240
it's an invariant manifold.

35:20.680 --> 35:21.740
Mathematically defining

35:21.740 --> 35:23.500
the absolute structural limits

35:23.500 --> 35:25.160
within which all control laws

35:25.160 --> 35:26.680
must operate

35:26.680 --> 35:27.720
to prevent the system

35:27.720 --> 35:28.800
from destroying itself.

35:28.940 --> 35:29.320
Correct.

35:29.320 --> 35:31.580
Ordinary, everyday laws

35:31.580 --> 35:32.880
like tax codes,

35:33.020 --> 35:33.640
speed limits,

35:33.740 --> 35:35.040
or environmental regulations

35:35.040 --> 35:36.560
are just localized

35:36.560 --> 35:37.620
control actions

35:37.620 --> 35:38.320
taking place

35:38.320 --> 35:39.380
inside the allowed

35:39.380 --> 35:40.320
safe space.

35:40.320 --> 35:41.540
But the constitution

35:41.540 --> 35:43.240
defines the rigid boundaries

35:43.240 --> 35:44.640
of the space itself.

35:44.760 --> 35:45.040
It says,

35:45.520 --> 35:47.160
you cannot steer past this point

35:47.160 --> 35:48.140
or the wings come off.

35:48.200 --> 35:48.700
Exactly.

35:49.100 --> 35:50.200
And this leads to

35:50.200 --> 35:50.940
what I think

35:50.940 --> 35:52.200
is the most provocative part

35:52.200 --> 35:53.140
of the entire monograph.

35:53.780 --> 35:55.220
It's a completely wild

35:55.220 --> 35:56.140
reinterpretation

35:56.140 --> 35:56.760
of human rights.

35:57.000 --> 35:57.820
It really challenges

35:57.820 --> 35:59.160
how we talk about rights.

35:59.460 --> 36:00.100
Because usually

36:00.100 --> 36:01.220
when we talk about human rights,

36:01.280 --> 36:02.520
we use one of two frameworks.

36:03.080 --> 36:04.440
We say rights are natural,

36:04.860 --> 36:06.100
God-given moral entitlement

36:06.100 --> 36:06.840
that you possess

36:06.840 --> 36:08.420
just by being born human.

36:08.560 --> 36:08.900
Or,

36:09.080 --> 36:10.380
if we are more legally minded,

36:10.780 --> 36:11.960
we say they are civic gifts

36:11.960 --> 36:12.920
granted by the state.

36:13.240 --> 36:14.180
But Flyxion says

36:14.180 --> 36:14.860
human rights

36:14.860 --> 36:16.500
are invariant constraints

36:16.500 --> 36:17.920
specifically designed

36:17.920 --> 36:18.480
to protect

36:18.480 --> 36:20.040
the distributed observer network.

36:20.340 --> 36:20.640
Yes.

36:21.300 --> 36:22.060
Let's look at

36:22.060 --> 36:23.140
some specific rights

36:23.140 --> 36:24.980
through this cybernetic lens

36:24.980 --> 36:25.620
because I want to see

36:25.620 --> 36:26.280
if this holds up.

36:26.640 --> 36:27.540
Let's start with

36:27.540 --> 36:28.480
freedom of speech.

36:28.480 --> 36:29.720
Under this framework,

36:29.900 --> 36:30.760
freedom of speech

36:30.760 --> 36:32.440
isn't just an abstract

36:32.440 --> 36:33.700
philosophical liberty

36:33.700 --> 36:34.820
to express yourself.

36:35.120 --> 36:36.200
It is the core

36:36.200 --> 36:37.500
mechanical mechanism

36:37.500 --> 36:38.320
that preserves

36:38.320 --> 36:39.040
the transmission

36:39.040 --> 36:40.000
of vital data

36:40.000 --> 36:41.040
throughout the entire

36:41.040 --> 36:42.020
estimation network.

36:42.080 --> 36:42.320
Right.

36:42.500 --> 36:43.580
If you restrict speech,

36:44.200 --> 36:45.400
the localized censors,

36:45.580 --> 36:46.040
the citizens,

36:46.380 --> 36:46.820
the journalists,

36:46.960 --> 36:47.400
the scientists,

36:47.900 --> 36:48.860
cannot send their data

36:48.860 --> 36:50.080
back to the central controller.

36:50.300 --> 36:51.560
The state goes blind.

36:51.700 --> 36:52.140
Exactly.

36:52.140 --> 36:53.300
What about due process?

36:53.940 --> 36:55.200
The right to a fair trial,

36:55.420 --> 36:55.860
a jury,

36:56.300 --> 36:57.160
a defense attorney?

36:57.360 --> 36:58.480
Due process acts

36:58.480 --> 37:00.720
as a required structural constraint

37:00.720 --> 37:02.780
on irreversible control actions.

37:02.920 --> 37:04.280
Explain what an irreversible

37:04.280 --> 37:05.380
control action is.

37:05.680 --> 37:06.440
When the government

37:06.440 --> 37:07.640
coerces someone,

37:08.040 --> 37:09.100
when it locks a citizen

37:09.100 --> 37:10.020
in a prison cell

37:10.020 --> 37:11.080
or executes them

37:11.080 --> 37:12.340
or seizes their property,

37:12.520 --> 37:13.740
that is a massive,

37:13.940 --> 37:14.660
highly localized

37:14.660 --> 37:15.580
control action.

37:15.620 --> 37:16.760
And you can't undo it easily.

37:17.160 --> 37:17.440
Right.

37:18.020 --> 37:19.440
Due process introduces

37:19.440 --> 37:21.480
a mandatory algorithmic delay

37:21.480 --> 37:22.920
and a multi-stage

37:22.920 --> 37:24.060
verification step

37:24.060 --> 37:24.760
to ensure that

37:24.760 --> 37:25.620
the state's estimate

37:25.620 --> 37:26.300
of reality,

37:26.980 --> 37:27.900
basically their belief

37:27.900 --> 37:28.400
that this person

37:28.400 --> 37:29.040
committed a crime,

37:29.380 --> 37:30.700
is actually accurate

37:30.700 --> 37:31.380
before the government

37:31.380 --> 37:32.520
is allowed to apply

37:32.520 --> 37:33.720
irreversible force.

37:33.940 --> 37:34.900
Let me try to deduce

37:34.900 --> 37:35.380
another one.

37:35.520 --> 37:35.980
Privacy.

37:36.780 --> 37:38.020
The right to be secure

37:38.020 --> 37:39.020
in your papers,

37:39.180 --> 37:39.580
your home,

37:39.660 --> 37:40.480
your digital data.

37:40.560 --> 37:40.940
Go for it.

37:41.340 --> 37:42.120
If the government

37:42.120 --> 37:42.920
needs data

37:42.920 --> 37:43.840
to steer the ship,

37:44.500 --> 37:45.240
shouldn't it theoretically

37:45.240 --> 37:45.980
want all the data?

37:46.680 --> 37:47.480
Total surveillance.

37:48.480 --> 37:48.980
But wait.

37:48.980 --> 37:50.020
If privacy is

37:50.020 --> 37:50.800
a fundamental right,

37:50.920 --> 37:51.540
it must serve

37:51.540 --> 37:52.460
a control function.

37:53.400 --> 37:53.900
Is privacy

37:53.900 --> 37:54.580
about preventing

37:54.580 --> 37:55.040
the center

37:55.040 --> 37:55.720
from overwhelming

37:55.720 --> 37:56.560
the local nodes?

37:56.820 --> 37:57.340
You hit the nail

37:57.340 --> 37:57.760
on the head.

37:57.940 --> 37:58.880
If the central controller

37:58.880 --> 37:59.760
tries to perfectly

37:59.760 --> 38:00.500
micromanage

38:00.500 --> 38:01.380
every single aspect

38:01.380 --> 38:02.000
of society,

38:02.140 --> 38:02.680
it will suffer

38:02.680 --> 38:03.420
from computational

38:03.420 --> 38:04.620
explosion and collapse.

38:04.760 --> 38:05.260
So privacy

38:05.260 --> 38:06.220
acts as a barrier

38:06.220 --> 38:06.900
that prevents

38:06.900 --> 38:07.880
the central controller

38:07.880 --> 38:08.780
from overriding

38:08.780 --> 38:09.580
local autonomy.

38:09.820 --> 38:10.380
It ensures

38:10.380 --> 38:11.120
that not every

38:11.120 --> 38:12.000
single aspect

38:12.000 --> 38:13.320
of the distributed network

38:13.320 --> 38:14.540
is perfectly legible

38:14.540 --> 38:15.140
to the center,

38:15.500 --> 38:16.320
which preserves

38:16.320 --> 38:17.100
the localized,

38:17.340 --> 38:17.920
decentralized

38:18.980 --> 38:20.280
that is absolutely

38:20.280 --> 38:21.740
necessary for complex

38:21.740 --> 38:22.620
modern society

38:22.620 --> 38:23.560
to function efficiently.

38:23.980 --> 38:24.700
Okay, I followed

38:24.700 --> 38:25.180
the logic,

38:25.580 --> 38:26.280
but I have to plant

38:26.280 --> 38:27.100
my flag here

38:27.100 --> 38:27.560
and push back

38:27.560 --> 38:28.280
hard on this.

38:29.140 --> 38:30.100
I'm feeling

38:30.100 --> 38:31.400
that unease again,

38:31.620 --> 38:33.680
but ten times stronger.

38:33.760 --> 38:34.220
I get it.

38:34.300 --> 38:35.080
It sounds cold again.

38:35.080 --> 38:35.880
This sounds

38:35.880 --> 38:36.980
incredibly,

38:37.200 --> 38:38.680
profoundly dystopian.

38:39.440 --> 38:40.040
Are we really

38:40.040 --> 38:40.820
sitting here saying

38:40.820 --> 38:41.720
that human rights,

38:42.360 --> 38:43.240
the right to exist,

38:43.360 --> 38:44.020
the right to speak,

38:44.100 --> 38:45.000
the right of a marginalized

38:45.000 --> 38:46.080
group to not be

38:46.080 --> 38:47.440
oppressed by a tyrant

38:47.440 --> 38:48.260
are just

38:48.260 --> 38:49.440
computational tools?

38:49.560 --> 38:50.100
I know.

38:50.220 --> 38:50.660
It sounds like

38:50.660 --> 38:51.300
we're stripping away

38:51.300 --> 38:51.860
the morality.

38:52.200 --> 38:53.300
That minority rights

38:53.300 --> 38:54.100
are just a convenient

38:54.100 --> 38:54.820
way to keep

38:54.820 --> 38:55.660
a math equation

38:55.660 --> 38:56.140
balanced.

38:56.580 --> 38:57.240
You're telling me

38:57.240 --> 38:58.120
that all the blood,

38:58.300 --> 38:58.980
sweat, and tears

38:58.980 --> 38:59.780
of the civil rights

38:59.780 --> 39:00.560
movement was just

39:00.560 --> 39:01.640
a fight for a

39:01.640 --> 39:02.420
higher dimensional

39:02.420 --> 39:03.400
state space.

39:04.060 --> 39:04.820
Doesn't this strip

39:04.820 --> 39:05.480
the absolute

39:05.480 --> 39:06.220
humanity,

39:06.480 --> 39:06.760
dignity,

39:06.760 --> 39:07.580
and morality

39:07.580 --> 39:09.000
out of justice?

39:09.620 --> 39:10.700
I cannot accept

39:10.700 --> 39:11.420
that human dignity

39:11.420 --> 39:12.280
is just a control

39:12.280 --> 39:12.720
parameter.

39:12.720 --> 39:13.500
That is the most

39:13.500 --> 39:14.360
important pushback

39:14.360 --> 39:14.940
you could offer,

39:15.080 --> 39:15.600
and it's a critique

39:15.600 --> 39:16.720
that any control

39:16.720 --> 39:17.440
theoretic view

39:17.440 --> 39:18.000
of society

39:18.000 --> 39:18.800
has to answer.

39:19.320 --> 39:19.980
But let's look

39:19.980 --> 39:20.460
at what happens

39:20.460 --> 39:21.740
when we rely solely

39:21.740 --> 39:22.980
on moral arguments

39:22.980 --> 39:23.820
for justice.

39:23.980 --> 39:24.780
Okay, let's look at it.

39:25.020 --> 39:25.900
Classical democratic

39:25.900 --> 39:26.640
theory actually

39:26.640 --> 39:27.660
struggles deeply

39:27.660 --> 39:28.360
with the concept

39:28.360 --> 39:29.420
of minority rights.

39:30.340 --> 39:30.960
If democracy

39:30.960 --> 39:31.720
is just about

39:31.720 --> 39:32.340
what the most

39:32.340 --> 39:33.120
people want,

39:33.560 --> 39:34.300
if it's pure

39:34.300 --> 39:35.380
majoritarianism,

39:35.840 --> 39:36.440
why shouldn't

39:36.440 --> 39:37.760
a 51% majority

39:37.760 --> 39:38.300
just be able

39:38.300 --> 39:38.980
to vote away

39:38.980 --> 39:39.440
the rights

39:39.440 --> 39:41.020
of the 49% minority?

39:41.260 --> 39:41.680
If the majority

39:41.680 --> 39:42.800
decides it's morally

39:42.800 --> 39:43.740
right to oppress

39:43.740 --> 39:44.300
a minority,

39:44.360 --> 39:45.320
the purely

39:45.320 --> 39:46.360
democratic argument

39:46.360 --> 39:47.280
runs into a wall.

39:47.440 --> 39:47.960
Exactly.

39:48.540 --> 39:49.260
Constitutional

39:49.260 --> 39:49.780
cybernetics

39:49.780 --> 39:50.600
doesn't replace

39:50.600 --> 39:51.480
the moral argument

39:51.480 --> 39:52.260
for human dignity.

39:52.880 --> 39:53.340
It provides

39:53.340 --> 39:54.220
an unbreakable

39:54.220 --> 39:55.540
structural reinforcement

39:55.540 --> 39:56.160
for it.

39:56.520 --> 39:57.100
It says that

39:57.100 --> 39:58.100
cognitive diversity

39:58.100 --> 39:59.000
is the ultimate

39:59.000 --> 40:00.280
non-renewable

40:00.280 --> 40:01.400
epistemic resource

40:01.400 --> 40:02.260
of a society.

40:02.480 --> 40:02.960
How so.

40:03.400 --> 40:04.040
Minorities,

40:04.220 --> 40:04.900
whether racial,

40:05.100 --> 40:05.400
religious,

40:05.620 --> 40:05.940
economic,

40:06.040 --> 40:06.720
or ideological,

40:07.440 --> 40:08.220
occupy parts

40:08.220 --> 40:08.940
of the societal

40:08.940 --> 40:09.680
state space

40:09.680 --> 40:10.420
that the majority

40:10.420 --> 40:11.800
literally cannot see.

40:12.080 --> 40:12.800
They have entirely

40:12.800 --> 40:13.340
different lived

40:13.340 --> 40:13.920
experiences,

40:14.160 --> 40:14.700
they interact

40:14.700 --> 40:15.380
with the state's

40:15.380 --> 40:16.080
coercive power

40:16.080 --> 40:16.560
differently,

40:16.880 --> 40:17.480
they sense

40:17.480 --> 40:18.200
different economic

40:18.200 --> 40:18.820
vulnerabilities,

40:18.820 --> 40:19.620
and they hold

40:19.620 --> 40:20.340
different cultural

40:20.340 --> 40:20.700
memories.

40:20.760 --> 40:21.400
So if a majority

40:21.400 --> 40:22.400
suppresses a minority

40:22.400 --> 40:22.780
group,

40:23.080 --> 40:23.720
they aren't just

40:23.720 --> 40:24.560
committing a moral

40:24.560 --> 40:25.060
sin,

40:25.420 --> 40:26.240
they are literally

40:26.240 --> 40:27.400
blinding the government

40:27.400 --> 40:29.020
to a huge section

40:29.020 --> 40:29.640
of reality.

40:30.020 --> 40:30.580
They are taking

40:30.580 --> 40:31.380
a sledgehammer

40:31.380 --> 40:32.000
to their own

40:32.000 --> 40:32.380
sensors.

40:32.780 --> 40:33.560
They are voluntarily

40:33.560 --> 40:34.640
reducing the

40:34.640 --> 40:35.400
dimensionality

40:35.400 --> 40:36.320
and the intelligence

40:36.320 --> 40:37.280
of the collective

40:37.280 --> 40:38.460
brain of society.

40:38.840 --> 40:40.300
And in a complex,

40:40.560 --> 40:41.440
rapidly changing

40:41.440 --> 40:41.980
world,

40:42.520 --> 40:43.540
a society with

40:43.540 --> 40:44.140
a reduced

40:44.140 --> 40:45.240
collective brain

40:45.240 --> 40:46.400
cannot survive

40:46.400 --> 40:46.960
for long.

40:47.520 --> 40:48.280
Oppression is

40:48.280 --> 40:49.540
fundamentally a form

40:49.540 --> 40:50.020
of censor

40:50.020 --> 40:50.520
destruction.

40:51.120 --> 40:51.740
A government

40:51.740 --> 40:53.040
that marginalizes

40:53.040 --> 40:53.780
its minorities,

40:53.980 --> 40:54.800
that locks them

40:54.800 --> 40:55.580
out of the voting

40:55.580 --> 40:56.780
booth or the economy,

40:57.320 --> 40:58.440
loses the ability

40:58.440 --> 41:00.040
to accurately estimate

41:00.040 --> 41:00.940
its true state.

41:01.540 --> 41:02.180
So justice

41:02.180 --> 41:02.960
and mathematical

41:02.960 --> 41:04.000
stability turn out

41:04.000 --> 41:04.560
to be exactly

41:04.560 --> 41:05.260
the same thing.

41:05.400 --> 41:06.060
You protect

41:06.060 --> 41:06.700
the minority

41:06.700 --> 41:07.660
not just because

41:07.660 --> 41:08.480
it is a nice

41:08.480 --> 41:09.820
moral thing to do,

41:09.940 --> 41:10.480
but because the

41:10.480 --> 41:11.400
basic survival

41:11.400 --> 41:12.220
of the entire

41:12.220 --> 41:13.500
constitutional system

41:13.500 --> 41:14.280
depends on

41:14.280 --> 41:15.120
preserving the

41:15.120 --> 41:16.160
absolute maximum

41:16.160 --> 41:16.900
diversity of

41:16.900 --> 41:17.500
observation.

41:18.420 --> 41:19.660
A tyrannical system

41:19.660 --> 41:20.520
is mathematically

41:20.520 --> 41:21.620
doomed to collapse

41:21.620 --> 41:22.380
because it cannot

41:22.380 --> 41:23.620
perceive the reality

41:23.620 --> 41:24.360
it is trying to

41:24.360 --> 41:24.720
control.

41:25.120 --> 41:25.800
That is a staggering

41:25.800 --> 41:26.580
way to look at it.

41:26.660 --> 41:26.840
Yeah.

41:26.920 --> 41:27.600
It actually makes

41:27.600 --> 41:28.380
the defense of

41:28.380 --> 41:28.940
human rights

41:28.940 --> 41:29.560
stronger.

41:30.040 --> 41:30.880
Because it removes

41:30.880 --> 41:31.760
the tyrant's excuse

41:31.760 --> 41:32.420
that oppression

41:32.420 --> 41:33.460
is necessary

41:33.460 --> 41:34.260
for stability.

41:34.700 --> 41:35.060
Oppression

41:35.060 --> 41:35.860
is instability.

41:36.300 --> 41:36.860
Okay, let's take

41:36.860 --> 41:37.160
stock.

41:37.820 --> 41:38.760
We know how the

41:38.760 --> 41:39.420
ship is steered

41:39.420 --> 41:39.820
through the

41:39.820 --> 41:40.540
cybernetic loop.

41:41.000 --> 41:41.640
We know the

41:41.640 --> 41:42.380
structural limits

41:42.380 --> 41:42.900
of the hull,

41:43.120 --> 41:43.460
which is the

41:43.460 --> 41:44.720
constitution acting

41:44.720 --> 41:45.480
as an invariant

41:45.480 --> 41:45.860
manifold.

41:46.360 --> 41:47.040
We know the

41:47.040 --> 41:47.660
censors are the

41:47.660 --> 41:48.500
citizens, the

41:48.500 --> 41:49.500
markets, and the

41:49.500 --> 41:50.720
scientists, protected

41:50.720 --> 41:51.420
by human rights.

41:51.900 --> 41:52.760
But there is a

41:52.760 --> 41:53.600
massive missing

41:53.600 --> 41:54.060
piece.

41:54.480 --> 41:55.420
Who decides the

41:55.420 --> 41:55.920
destination?

41:56.180 --> 41:56.820
Who sets the

41:56.820 --> 41:57.160
GPS?

41:57.560 --> 41:58.260
Think back to the

41:58.260 --> 41:59.200
thermostat analogy.

41:59.200 --> 42:00.720
A thermostat is a

42:00.720 --> 42:01.400
brilliant control

42:01.400 --> 42:02.440
system, but it has

42:02.440 --> 42:03.340
no free will.

42:03.680 --> 42:04.580
It doesn't wake up

42:04.580 --> 42:05.300
and decide what the

42:05.300 --> 42:05.820
temperature of the

42:05.820 --> 42:06.340
room should be.

42:06.720 --> 42:07.860
A human being walks

42:07.860 --> 42:08.980
up to it and sets it

42:08.980 --> 42:10.300
to 72 degrees.

42:10.400 --> 42:11.780
The 72 degrees is an

42:11.780 --> 42:12.660
external reference

42:12.660 --> 42:13.000
point.

42:13.240 --> 42:14.200
But human societies

42:14.200 --> 42:15.420
have no external

42:15.420 --> 42:15.880
engineer.

42:16.420 --> 42:17.300
There is no outside

42:17.300 --> 42:18.920
force, no alien race

42:18.920 --> 42:19.920
telling us what the

42:19.920 --> 42:20.980
perfect society looks

42:20.980 --> 42:21.300
like.

42:21.680 --> 42:22.680
Therefore, we have to

42:22.680 --> 42:23.520
estimate our own

42:23.520 --> 42:24.460
desired destination

42:24.460 --> 42:25.220
from within.

42:25.980 --> 42:26.940
Flakeshin calls this

42:26.940 --> 42:28.060
process adaptive

42:28.060 --> 42:29.160
reference estimation.

42:30.040 --> 42:30.440
So while the

42:30.440 --> 42:31.140
everyday government

42:31.140 --> 42:32.020
bureaucracy is

42:32.020 --> 42:32.720
estimating the

42:32.720 --> 42:33.320
current state of

42:33.320 --> 42:34.580
society, how many

42:34.580 --> 42:36.000
people are sick, how

42:36.000 --> 42:36.760
much money is in the

42:36.760 --> 42:38.840
bank, democracy is

42:38.840 --> 42:39.520
the higher level

42:39.520 --> 42:40.680
process of estimating

42:40.680 --> 42:41.640
the desired reference

42:41.640 --> 42:42.260
trajectory.

42:42.760 --> 42:43.040
Exactly.

42:43.240 --> 42:44.240
It's how we update

42:44.240 --> 42:45.280
the ultimate goals of

42:45.280 --> 42:46.820
society based on new

42:46.820 --> 42:47.980
science, new moral

42:47.980 --> 42:49.060
awakenings, new

42:49.060 --> 42:50.300
technology, and

42:50.300 --> 42:51.180
cultural shifts.

42:51.180 --> 42:52.140
This reframes

42:52.140 --> 42:53.380
democracy entirely.

42:54.260 --> 42:55.280
Democracy is not just

42:55.280 --> 42:56.380
a mechanical procedure

42:56.380 --> 42:57.580
for picking which

42:57.580 --> 42:58.880
politician gets to sit

42:58.880 --> 42:59.760
in a leather chair for

42:59.760 --> 43:00.400
four years.

43:00.860 --> 43:01.880
It is a massive

43:01.880 --> 43:03.880
society-wide recursive

43:03.880 --> 43:04.740
process of goal

43:04.740 --> 43:05.060
finding.

43:05.520 --> 43:06.560
Elections, public

43:06.560 --> 43:07.780
debates, street

43:07.780 --> 43:09.300
protests, investigative

43:09.300 --> 43:10.460
journalism, art,

43:10.940 --> 43:12.660
culture, these are all

43:12.660 --> 43:14.120
mechanisms for the

43:14.120 --> 43:15.600
distributed observer

43:15.600 --> 43:17.320
network to collectively

43:17.320 --> 43:18.380
calibrate the compass.

43:18.800 --> 43:19.640
Because the reference

43:19.640 --> 43:20.760
trajectory of a society

43:20.760 --> 43:21.700
has to evolve.

43:22.140 --> 43:22.780
Think about how the

43:22.780 --> 43:23.940
scientific discovery of

43:23.940 --> 43:25.380
germ theory or the

43:25.380 --> 43:26.080
invention of the

43:26.080 --> 43:27.360
internet or the moral

43:27.360 --> 43:28.100
awakening of the

43:28.100 --> 43:28.760
civil rights movement

43:28.760 --> 43:30.320
completely changed what

43:30.320 --> 43:31.520
society deemed as its

43:31.520 --> 43:32.340
desired future.

43:32.540 --> 43:33.360
Democracy is the

43:33.360 --> 43:34.380
algorithm that allows

43:34.380 --> 43:35.400
the system to change

43:35.400 --> 43:36.560
its own goals without

43:36.560 --> 43:37.580
destroying itself.

43:37.680 --> 43:38.420
So what does this all

43:38.420 --> 43:39.160
mean for the listener

43:39.160 --> 43:39.880
when they go to the

43:39.880 --> 43:40.380
ballot box?

43:40.520 --> 43:41.720
It means voting isn't a

43:41.720 --> 43:42.720
multiple choice test where

43:42.720 --> 43:43.440
you just pick the winner

43:43.440 --> 43:44.040
and go home.

43:44.040 --> 43:44.920
It's a continuous

43:44.920 --> 43:45.820
calibration of the

43:45.820 --> 43:46.100
system.

43:46.280 --> 43:47.300
But this leads to a

43:47.300 --> 43:47.780
question about

43:47.780 --> 43:48.360
legitimacy.

43:49.200 --> 43:50.680
If legitimacy isn't

43:50.680 --> 43:51.620
just about the fact that

43:51.620 --> 43:52.880
we held an election or

43:52.880 --> 43:54.220
the historical idea that

43:54.220 --> 43:55.860
our ancestors signed a

43:55.860 --> 43:56.860
social contract like

43:56.860 --> 43:57.880
John Locke talked about,

43:58.340 --> 43:59.380
what actually makes a

43:59.380 --> 44:00.080
government legitimate

44:00.080 --> 44:00.560
today?

44:00.960 --> 44:01.880
Legitimacy gets a

44:01.880 --> 44:03.020
fascinating geometric

44:03.020 --> 44:04.320
reformulation in this

44:04.320 --> 44:04.720
text.

44:05.300 --> 44:06.320
Flyxion argues that a

44:06.320 --> 44:07.180
government is legitimate

44:07.180 --> 44:09.020
if and only if it

44:09.020 --> 44:10.780
preserves or expands the

44:10.780 --> 44:12.520
future reachability, the

44:12.520 --> 44:14.120
future option sets of its

44:14.120 --> 44:15.220
distributed observers.

44:15.920 --> 44:17.020
In other words, do the

44:17.020 --> 44:17.980
actions of the state

44:17.980 --> 44:18.980
expand the possible

44:18.980 --> 44:20.240
futures available to the

44:20.240 --> 44:21.420
citizens or do they

44:21.420 --> 44:22.060
collapse them?

44:22.060 --> 44:23.060
Which provides a

44:23.060 --> 44:24.120
mathematical definition

44:24.120 --> 44:24.960
of coercion.

44:25.400 --> 44:26.560
Coercion is defined here

44:26.560 --> 44:27.400
as the unnecessary

44:27.400 --> 44:28.940
collapse of a citizen's

44:28.940 --> 44:30.120
future trajectories.

44:30.280 --> 44:31.220
If the state arrests you

44:31.220 --> 44:32.260
and locks you in a cage

44:32.260 --> 44:33.960
without due process, your

44:33.960 --> 44:35.120
infinite future reachable

44:35.120 --> 44:36.300
states just violently

44:36.300 --> 44:37.400
shrank to the physical

44:37.400 --> 44:38.580
size of a jail cell.

44:39.060 --> 44:40.120
That is pure coercion.

44:40.400 --> 44:41.880
But if the state taxes

44:41.880 --> 44:43.440
you, which some people view

44:43.440 --> 44:45.320
as coercion, to build a

44:45.320 --> 44:46.680
public university system,

44:47.240 --> 44:48.240
they might be slightly

44:48.240 --> 44:49.260
reducing your personal

44:49.260 --> 44:50.740
financial trajectory today,

44:50.860 --> 44:52.400
but they are massively,

44:52.840 --> 44:54.560
exponentially expanding the

44:54.560 --> 44:56.020
future reachable trajectories

44:56.020 --> 44:57.260
of millions of students,

44:57.760 --> 44:58.820
increasing the overall

44:58.820 --> 45:00.000
maneuverability and

45:00.000 --> 45:01.440
intelligence of the entire

45:01.440 --> 45:02.120
society.

45:02.260 --> 45:02.860
Exactly.

45:03.700 --> 45:04.720
Legitimacy isn't about

45:04.720 --> 45:05.800
looking backward at

45:05.800 --> 45:06.820
historical consent.

45:07.460 --> 45:08.200
It isn't about whether

45:08.200 --> 45:09.700
people 200 years ago

45:09.700 --> 45:10.700
agreed to a document.

45:11.420 --> 45:12.740
Legitimacy is entirely about

45:12.740 --> 45:13.640
preserving future

45:13.640 --> 45:14.260
continuation.

45:14.260 --> 45:16.040
A legitimate system ensures

45:16.040 --> 45:17.140
that the people living in it

45:17.140 --> 45:18.640
today have the capacity

45:18.640 --> 45:20.200
to keep adapting, keep

45:20.200 --> 45:21.320
learning, and keep

45:21.320 --> 45:22.260
correcting their course

45:22.260 --> 45:22.660
tomorrow.

45:22.780 --> 45:23.480
But even the most

45:23.480 --> 45:25.260
legitimate, most well-designed

45:25.260 --> 45:26.360
cybernetic systems can

45:26.360 --> 45:26.720
crash.

45:26.940 --> 45:28.040
We see it in history all the

45:28.040 --> 45:28.300
time.

45:28.660 --> 45:29.420
Empires fall.

45:29.740 --> 45:30.600
Democracies crumble.

45:31.040 --> 45:32.320
If this control loop is so

45:32.320 --> 45:33.780
elegant, why does it fail?

45:34.180 --> 45:35.340
Because human institutions

45:35.340 --> 45:37.100
are built on fragile, noisy

45:37.100 --> 45:37.720
foundations.

45:38.460 --> 45:39.980
Systems rarely fail overnight

45:39.980 --> 45:41.180
in a sudden explosion.

45:41.820 --> 45:43.400
They fail through cascading,

45:43.400 --> 45:45.040
positive feedback loops of

45:45.040 --> 45:46.020
estimation errors.

45:46.460 --> 45:48.080
It's a slow accumulation of

45:48.080 --> 45:48.380
rot.

45:48.600 --> 45:49.300
What are the main failure

45:49.300 --> 45:49.620
modes?

45:49.980 --> 45:51.560
The text identifies several

45:51.560 --> 45:52.980
key failure modes that should

45:52.980 --> 45:54.540
sound terrifyingly familiar.

45:55.400 --> 45:56.380
First, there is

45:56.380 --> 45:57.360
observational delay.

45:57.940 --> 45:58.860
This is when the government

45:58.860 --> 46:00.240
is making critical decisions

46:00.240 --> 46:01.820
based on data that is six

46:01.820 --> 46:03.220
months or two years old.

46:03.500 --> 46:04.700
By the time the control

46:04.700 --> 46:06.220
action is applied, the

46:06.220 --> 46:07.720
reality has already moved on

46:07.720 --> 46:09.860
and the cure actually harms

46:09.860 --> 46:10.620
the new reality.

46:10.800 --> 46:12.080
Second, there is distortion,

46:12.320 --> 46:12.960
which we talked about

46:12.960 --> 46:13.340
earlier.

46:13.760 --> 46:15.420
The sensors become biased or

46:15.420 --> 46:16.760
corrupted by political pressure,

46:17.280 --> 46:19.140
constantly feeding bad,

46:19.320 --> 46:20.780
artificially rosy data into

46:20.780 --> 46:21.580
the control loop.

46:21.940 --> 46:23.140
Third, there is semantic

46:23.140 --> 46:23.640
drift.

46:24.320 --> 46:25.240
This is insidious.

46:25.920 --> 46:27.480
The Babel protocol completely

46:27.480 --> 46:28.160
breaks down.

46:28.820 --> 46:29.980
Institutions use the same

46:29.980 --> 46:31.680
words, but the words lose all

46:31.680 --> 46:32.620
connection to reality.

46:32.780 --> 46:33.920
I want to pause on semantic

46:33.920 --> 46:35.080
drift because I think I've seen

46:35.080 --> 46:35.960
this happen in real life.

46:36.300 --> 46:37.240
Let's look at a massive

46:37.240 --> 46:38.140
healthcare bureaucracy.

46:39.020 --> 46:40.500
They might define quality of

46:40.500 --> 46:42.520
care as a specific set of

46:42.520 --> 46:43.420
measurable outcomes.

46:43.600 --> 46:45.240
Let's say how fast a patient

46:45.240 --> 46:46.080
is discharged.

46:46.600 --> 46:47.680
Over time, the hospital

46:47.680 --> 46:49.280
administrators become obsessed

46:49.280 --> 46:49.920
with the metric.

46:50.340 --> 46:51.700
They optimize everything to get

46:51.700 --> 46:53.520
patients out the door faster to

46:53.520 --> 46:54.640
make the numbers look good.

46:54.960 --> 46:56.920
And the metric of quality of

46:56.920 --> 46:59.240
care drifts away from actual

46:59.240 --> 47:01.180
human health and becomes purely

47:01.180 --> 47:02.680
about administrative speed.

47:03.240 --> 47:05.000
The institution thinks it's

47:05.000 --> 47:06.500
succeeding wildly because the

47:06.500 --> 47:07.820
chart is going up, but the

47:07.820 --> 47:09.660
actual patients are dying at

47:09.660 --> 47:09.980
home.

47:10.280 --> 47:11.760
That is the perfect example of

47:11.760 --> 47:12.560
semantic drift.

47:13.340 --> 47:15.200
The map completely detaches from

47:15.200 --> 47:16.420
the territory, but the

47:16.420 --> 47:18.700
institution keeps worshiping the

47:18.700 --> 47:18.960
map.

47:19.300 --> 47:21.480
And the final major failure mode is

47:21.480 --> 47:22.940
institutional memory loss.

47:23.640 --> 47:25.400
The system literally forgets how

47:25.400 --> 47:27.160
it solved complex problems in the

47:27.160 --> 47:27.600
past.

47:27.920 --> 47:29.500
The experienced engineers retire.

47:29.980 --> 47:31.360
The old pandemic playbooks are

47:31.360 --> 47:32.180
thrown in the trash.

47:32.600 --> 47:33.860
The cultural knowledge of how to

47:33.860 --> 47:35.340
build infrastructure is lost.

47:35.500 --> 47:37.280
When a crisis hits, the system has

47:37.280 --> 47:39.820
to painfully reinvent the wheel, and

47:39.820 --> 47:41.080
it usually doesn't have the time to

47:41.080 --> 47:42.420
do so before it crashes.

47:42.740 --> 47:44.500
And when all these errors, the

47:44.500 --> 47:46.160
delay, the distortion, the drift,

47:46.240 --> 47:48.200
the amnesia accumulate, the

47:48.200 --> 47:49.760
system starts to lose a critical

47:49.760 --> 47:51.660
property called Lyapunov stability.

47:51.900 --> 47:52.200
Yes.

47:52.580 --> 47:54.420
Lyapunov stability is a profound

47:54.420 --> 47:56.320
concept from dynamical systems

47:56.320 --> 47:56.700
theory.

47:57.280 --> 47:58.900
True stability doesn't mean standing

47:58.900 --> 48:00.460
perfectly still like a statue.

48:00.760 --> 48:01.940
It doesn't mean a society never

48:01.940 --> 48:03.820
faces crises or never wobbles.

48:04.320 --> 48:06.020
Stability means that when the system

48:06.020 --> 48:08.680
is disturbed, hit by a massive shock

48:08.680 --> 48:10.400
like a recession or a natural

48:10.400 --> 48:12.900
disaster, the resulting trajectory

48:12.900 --> 48:15.080
remains bounded within a recoverable

48:15.080 --> 48:15.540
region.

48:16.200 --> 48:18.400
It might wobble violently, but the

48:18.400 --> 48:19.980
control loops eventually pull it back

48:19.980 --> 48:20.480
to safety.

48:20.820 --> 48:21.660
It stabilizes.

48:22.080 --> 48:24.260
A loss of Lyapunov stability means the

48:24.260 --> 48:26.300
system has entered a state where every

48:26.300 --> 48:28.100
single correction the government makes,

48:28.180 --> 48:29.640
no matter how well intentioned,

48:29.960 --> 48:32.000
actually pushes the system further away

48:32.000 --> 48:33.500
from safety.

48:33.500 --> 48:35.160
The feedback loop turns negative.

48:35.660 --> 48:37.580
It's like a driver hitting a patch of

48:37.580 --> 48:38.840
black ice on the highway.

48:39.380 --> 48:40.680
The car starts sliding left.

48:40.880 --> 48:42.880
The driver panics and yanks the steering

48:42.880 --> 48:44.040
wheel hard to the right.

48:44.400 --> 48:46.100
The tires catch for a second, but because

48:46.100 --> 48:47.880
they overcorrected, the car snaps and

48:47.880 --> 48:49.440
slides even faster to the right.

48:49.900 --> 48:51.480
So they yank the wheel back left.

48:51.920 --> 48:53.640
The oscillations get bigger and bigger until

48:53.640 --> 48:55.180
the car spins out into the ditch.

48:55.320 --> 48:57.200
The driver's attempts to save the car are

48:57.200 --> 48:58.580
exactly what caused the crash.

48:58.580 --> 49:00.380
And in government, according to

49:00.380 --> 49:02.500
Flyxion, this societal spin-out is

49:02.500 --> 49:04.080
usually caused by something called

49:04.080 --> 49:05.440
model rigidity.

49:05.840 --> 49:08.200
Model rigidity is a deadly disease for

49:08.200 --> 49:08.720
governments.

49:09.480 --> 49:12.080
Institutions become incredibly arrogantly

49:12.080 --> 49:13.940
confident in the models that brought them

49:13.940 --> 49:15.060
success in the past.

49:15.540 --> 49:17.520
They cling to them like religious dogma.

49:18.040 --> 49:20.280
But the environment is always mutating.

49:20.620 --> 49:22.540
Imagine an administration trying to

49:22.540 --> 49:25.660
regulate the 21st century digital economy.

49:26.300 --> 49:27.820
Artificial intelligence, cryptocurrency,

49:27.820 --> 49:31.440
gig work using the analog, 1930s bureaucratic

49:31.440 --> 49:33.740
models designed for factories, and radio

49:33.740 --> 49:34.380
broadcasting.

49:34.600 --> 49:36.660
The institutions refuse to update their

49:36.660 --> 49:38.700
representations of reality, so they keep

49:38.700 --> 49:40.760
applying regulatory control actions that

49:40.760 --> 49:41.960
used to work in 1935.

49:42.340 --> 49:44.980
But today, those exact same actions have

49:44.980 --> 49:47.740
totally unintended disastrous consequences

49:47.740 --> 49:50.320
because the underlying reality has shifted.

49:50.400 --> 49:51.820
They turn in the steering wheel, but the

49:51.820 --> 49:53.240
rudder is no longer in the water.

49:53.400 --> 49:55.080
And here's the really terrifying part, the

49:55.080 --> 49:56.400
thing that will keep me up at night.

49:56.400 --> 49:59.860
A perfectly constitutional, legally compliant

49:59.860 --> 50:02.540
government can still utterly collapse.

50:02.860 --> 50:04.560
It can obey every single law in the books,

50:05.120 --> 50:07.060
follow every bureaucratic procedure, hold

50:07.060 --> 50:09.060
every election right on time, and still

50:09.060 --> 50:12.580
completely lose Lepunov stability if it slowly

50:12.580 --> 50:14.720
exhausts its future maneuverability through

50:14.720 --> 50:15.560
model rigidity.

50:15.960 --> 50:18.100
Legality does not equal stability.

50:18.600 --> 50:21.880
You can legally, meticulously, constitutionally,

50:22.180 --> 50:23.740
drive your car straight off a cliff.

50:23.740 --> 50:26.200
We have to break the illusion of SACI and

50:26.200 --> 50:26.640
procedure.

50:27.340 --> 50:29.740
A constitutional crisis isn't always a dramatic

50:29.740 --> 50:32.060
military coup d'etat with tanks in the

50:32.060 --> 50:32.360
streets.

50:32.580 --> 50:35.120
It is far more often this silent, invisible

50:35.120 --> 50:37.020
contraction of the admissible region.

50:37.560 --> 50:40.340
It is the slow exhaustion of options until

50:40.340 --> 50:43.000
disturbances that used to be easily absorbed

50:43.000 --> 50:45.800
by the society become unrecoverable shocks.

50:45.800 --> 50:49.360
The control authority quietly saturates.

50:49.780 --> 50:51.600
The government is issuing commands, the politicians

50:51.600 --> 50:53.780
are giving speeches, the courts are passing down

50:53.780 --> 50:56.720
rulings, but the ship is no longer responding to

50:56.720 --> 50:57.140
the rudder.

50:57.460 --> 51:00.000
It is just drifting on the current toward the rocks.

51:00.340 --> 51:01.520
That's a sobering thought.

51:01.880 --> 51:04.020
Okay, let's take a deep breath and zoom all the way out.

51:04.560 --> 51:07.300
We've been on a seriously mind-bending journey today.

51:07.640 --> 51:10.000
We started standing in an empty field, looking at a

51:10.000 --> 51:12.200
blank slate, asking how to build a government.

51:12.200 --> 51:14.360
And we've learned that government isn't a static

51:14.360 --> 51:16.640
authority sitting on a throne issuing moral

51:16.640 --> 51:17.060
commands.

51:17.320 --> 51:20.360
It is a living, breathing, desperately vulnerable

51:20.360 --> 51:21.980
cybernetic feedback loop.

51:22.340 --> 51:25.900
It is a massive decentralized network of censors.

51:26.360 --> 51:29.460
You, me, the financial markets, the courtrooms, the

51:29.460 --> 51:32.280
scientific laboratories, all desperately trying to

51:32.280 --> 51:35.820
translate messy data bound by the rigid structural

51:35.820 --> 51:38.680
limits of a constitution, trying to steer the human

51:38.680 --> 51:41.240
trajectory toward a future that preserves our

51:41.240 --> 51:41.760
possibilities.

51:41.760 --> 51:44.280
I think the ultimate takeaway here is that we have to

51:44.280 --> 51:46.780
fundamentally change how we evaluate our societies.

51:47.400 --> 51:49.660
We have to stop judging our governments by asking if they

51:49.660 --> 51:53.560
have achieved some perfect, final, utopian state, because

51:53.560 --> 51:55.100
that state does not exist.

51:55.580 --> 51:58.620
We have to evaluate them by asking if they retain the

51:58.620 --> 52:01.200
capacity to keep correcting their inevitable errors.

52:01.460 --> 52:03.560
Do we still have a working steering wheel?

52:03.880 --> 52:07.320
Are our censors or journalists or minorities or scientists

52:07.320 --> 52:10.600
still allowed to tell the absolute truth about what they see?

52:10.600 --> 52:15.340
Are we preserving the future option space or are we burning it to stay warm

52:15.340 --> 52:15.620
today?

52:15.620 --> 52:17.020
I want you to look around tomorrow.

52:17.020 --> 52:18.500
I want you to look around tomorrow, look at the morning news, look at the

52:18.500 --> 52:22.740
fluctuations of the stock market, read about the latest Supreme Court rulings, and even

52:22.740 --> 52:25.980
look at your own messy conversations with your neighbors on social media.

52:26.520 --> 52:30.000
Try not to see them as just isolated, frustrating political events.

52:30.400 --> 52:35.660
Try to see them as millions of specialized sensors pinging raw, vital data back to the central

52:35.660 --> 52:42.220
processor, all of us trying to keep the human trajectory viable in a chaotic, unpredictable

52:42.220 --> 52:42.780
universe.

52:42.780 --> 52:45.660
You aren't just a passive citizen waiting to be ruled.

52:45.940 --> 52:50.100
You are a vital, load-bearing node in the estimation network.

52:50.160 --> 52:50.640
Absolutely.

52:51.040 --> 52:53.820
And I'll leave you with this final provocative thought to chew on.

52:53.820 --> 53:00.800
If democracy is the algorithm we use to update our society's GPS, and new technology like

53:00.800 --> 53:06.760
artificial intelligence is currently extending our state space, creating entirely new trajectories,

53:07.100 --> 53:11.940
new realities, and new existential threats faster than human cognition can even comprehend,

53:12.520 --> 53:17.340
is our current human speed babble protocol actually capable of translating this new reality?

53:17.340 --> 53:23.420
Or are we standing at the helm navigating a hyper-complex 21st century ocean with a 19th century wooden

53:23.420 --> 53:23.920
compass?

53:24.240 --> 53:28.340
Think about that the next time you cast a vote, read a headline, or look out at that vast,

53:28.460 --> 53:30.360
unpredictable ocean we were all sailing together.

